WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:00.947
From a plane,

2
00:00:00.947 --> 00:00:02.665
you sometimes see a lake shaped like

3
00:00:02.665 --> 00:00:05.486
a horseshoe, right beside a river.

4
00:00:05.486 --> 00:00:06.543
The river made it,

5
00:00:06.543 --> 00:00:08.352
and then left it behind.

6
00:00:08.752 --> 00:00:09.576
On a flat plain,

7
00:00:09.576 --> 00:00:11.759
a river does not run straight.

8
00:00:11.759 --> 00:00:13.326
It swings from side to side in

9
00:00:13.326 --> 00:00:15.414
loops called meanders.

10
00:00:15.814 --> 00:00:17.103
On the outside of each bend,

11
00:00:17.103 --> 00:00:18.519
the water is fast and eats into

12
00:00:18.519 --> 00:00:19.587
the bank.

13
00:00:19.587 --> 00:00:20.377
On the inside,

14
00:00:20.377 --> 00:00:21.863
it slows down and drops sand and

15
00:00:21.863 --> 00:00:22.801
silt.

16
00:00:23.202 --> 00:00:24.235
Year after year,

17
00:00:24.235 --> 00:00:26.151
the loop grows deeper and its neck

18
00:00:26.151 --> 00:00:27.416
gets narrower.

19
00:00:27.416 --> 00:00:28.171
In the end,

20
00:00:28.171 --> 00:00:30.282
the river cuts straight across the neck.

21
00:00:30.682 --> 00:00:32.470
The old loop is sealed off.

22
00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:34.409
What remains is a curved lake,

23
00:00:34.409 --> 00:00:35.872
cut off from the river.

24
00:00:35.872 --> 00:00:37.809
That is an oxbow lake.

25
00:00:38.208 --> 00:00:39.369
Seen from a satellite,

26
00:00:39.369 --> 00:00:40.971
old floodplains are full of them,

27
00:00:40.971 --> 00:00:42.411
a record of where the river used

28
00:00:42.411 --> 00:00:43.477
to flow.

29
00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:44.806
For GS One:

30
00:00:44.806 --> 00:00:46.083
erosion on the concave bank,

31
00:00:46.083 --> 00:00:47.418
deposition on the convex bank,

32
00:00:47.418 --> 00:00:49.519
a cut-off, and an oxbow lake.

33
00:00:49.519 --> 00:00:51.375
Draw it as four steps.

